WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.600
Hey guys, Pete here. today i'm going to
explain the ending of Lovecraft Country

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.120
season 1 episode 2.
to do that i'm going to rely heavily on

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.480
the book of the same name that the show
is based on. there was a lot of

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.640
information crammed into the second
episode which was titled "whitey's on the

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.279
moon"
and based on the reactions i've seen it

00:00:19.279 --> 00:00:22.800
was confusing for some viewers.
having read the book i didn't really

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.480
have trouble following along with what
was happening but there were some big

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.119
changes between the book and show that
got me thinking.

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:32.880
so i thought doing an explainer video to
fill in some details from the book

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.559
while looking at the changes that were
made would be the best video to make

00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:39.840
this week.
as far as spoilers this video will

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.960
discuss everything that happened in the
first two episodes

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.440
and the book up into that same point. i
won't spoil the ending of the story

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.440
or any of the major plot stuff that
happens after the trip to Ardham

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.879
to rescue Montrose. episode 2
picks up right where episode 1 left off

00:00:56.879 --> 00:01:00.640
Tic, Leti, and George
made it to Ardham in one piece and we

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.280
learned that this giant estate they
arrived at

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.760
is owned by the Braithwhite family we
meet two members of the family

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.840
Samuel and his daughter Christina we
also learned that the Braithwhites are

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.960
tied to a secret society and that
Atticus

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.520
is a distant relative of theirs through
one of his mother's ancestors named

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:23.040
Hannah.
William the mysterious manservant of the

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.000
house explains the history of it all
like this.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.360
a distant cousin of Samuel's, Titus
Braithwhite

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.280
built the original estate which burned
down during the autumnal

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:38.560
equinox of 1833. the fire killed Titus
and everyone inside

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:43.200
except for one of his slaves. that slave
turned out to be Hannah who was pregnant

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.240
with his child
and that's how Tic ended up being a

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.640
direct descendant of the Braithwhites
this is largely the same as what's in

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.520
the book but things play out differently
in the show.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.200
the main difference being that Tic
already knows about Hannah

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.680
in the book rather than George playing a
key role and figuring out what's going

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.159
on
from there we get a lot of changes.

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:09.520
Christina is actually gender swapped.
in the book her character is Samuel's son

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:12.959
who's named Caleb.
this changes the tension she has with

00:02:12.959 --> 00:02:15.520
her father
but beyond that it doesn't make a big

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:18.879
difference at this point and the
character seems like it works pretty

00:02:18.879 --> 00:02:22.000
well with abby lee in the role so i
think it's fine. her

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.440
father is the current leader of a sect
of the order of the ancient dawn. this

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.120
name is slightly different as it
includes the word adamite in it - the

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:35.519
adamite order of the ancient dawn. the
adamites were a real group of early

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:37.440
christians you can look up if you want
to

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.840
but i think the explanation samuel gave
to atticus is all you need to know.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:45.280
he wants to return to paradise or regain
the primeval

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.920
innocence of man and in the process
achieve immortality. this was the same

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.760
thing titus was trying to do when he
burned down the original lodge.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:58.640
titus used spells from the book of names
to make his body more powerful.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:03.280
since tic is his last remaining blood
heir he's a reservoir of that power.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:07.680
samuel thinks he can step into the
garden of eden and achieve immortality

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.640
using that power
as part of his spell. as far as the other

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:16.239
men we see at the dinner
george explains that the order of the

00:03:16.239 --> 00:03:20.480
ancient dawn has lodges all
across the country. the brathwhites lodge

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.159
is called the sons of adam
and samuel has basically called in all

00:03:24.159 --> 00:03:27.440
the other leaders of all the other
lodges to be there

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:32.080
to witness this ceremony. christina's
remark that her father's associates

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.159
would never fraternize with the klan
because they're too poor gives you an

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:39.200
idea of how rich and powerful the
members of this order

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.080
are. they're able to cast spells which we
see several examples of in the episode

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.519
and naturally they believe they are
superior to normal people.

00:03:47.519 --> 00:03:52.000
this extends to white supremacy as
george mentioned they don't accept

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.720
non-whites into the order as well.
the ceremony and the lead up to it is

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:01.280
different in the show and to be honest
i'm not sure it's entirely clear what

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.159
happened. christina mentions the language
of adam

00:04:04.159 --> 00:04:07.920
and her father uses it during the
ceremony to cast his spell.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:11.920
in the book tic is told that he's going
to have to speak the language of adam

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.920
even though he's never heard it. samuel
explains that everyone knows it we just

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.000
don't remember that we do.
once things get started it does come to

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:24.240
him and as he starts to speak it he
starts to understand what's happening.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:27.680
he realizes that he will stop existing
as he is

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:32.000
once he's done his part in the ritual.
basically that they want to use his

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.919
power and it will use it up
and he'll just sort of transfer over

00:04:35.919 --> 00:04:39.440
into oblivion. this isn't something he's
interested in doing

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:43.600
and the twist is that he received a note
with writing in the language of adam on

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.600
it earlier in the day
that said to read it once he could. he

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.479
does that
and in the process he's protected from

00:04:50.479 --> 00:04:54.560
the light that kills everyone else in
the room and turns them to ash.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:59.120
more or less what we saw happen on the
show only it's not clear how or why

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:03.520
he was protected there. what we see in
the show is that samuel is speaking the

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:06.560
language of adam
and things seem to be working until

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:10.560
something happens with tic's ring.
christina gave him that so she may have

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.120
put a spell on it and this would make
sense

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.199
since the note with the language of adam
he got in the book came from samuel's

00:05:17.199 --> 00:05:19.759
son.
it's not clear though and to make things

00:05:19.759 --> 00:05:23.120
more confusing
he sees a pregnant hannah in the portal

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:26.320
after it opens up which didn't happen in
the book either.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:30.479
does that mean her presence somehow
protected tic? i just don't know.

00:05:30.479 --> 00:05:33.600
she does also lead him out of the
collapsing house though

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:37.280
so at the very least she was there for
that. it should be noted that she's

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:41.840
carrying a book with her as she goes
and this is most likely the book of

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:45.840
names which was
mentioned a few times in the episode. so

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:50.000
to recap the differences
in the book atticus makes a decision to

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:54.240
save himself by reading some words
during the ceremony that were given to

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:58.319
him by samuel braithwight's son.
there's no ticking clock situation

00:05:58.319 --> 00:06:02.240
because george and leti hadn't been
shot and hannah doesn't appear during

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:05.600
the ceremony.
in the show tic is less of an active

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:08.800
participant. as samuel
is opening the door to the garden of

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:13.520
eden the ring that christina gave him
seems to protect him while the sons of

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:16.639
adam are killed.
hannah appears to him and he follows her

00:06:16.639 --> 00:06:21.440
to safety as the lodge collapses.
outside he learns that uncle george died

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.440
which is the biggest change from the
book.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:27.680
this is actually a real head scratcher
because without giving away any details

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.800
george plays an important role with
things later in the book.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:35.759
it's also weird that the show decided to
add the possibility that george might be

00:06:35.759 --> 00:06:39.520
tic's biological father
since none of this is in the book. we can

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:44.000
only speculate but my guess is that
the show is going to use that connection

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.919
to bring george back.
i mean i do think he's dead. i think a

00:06:47.919 --> 00:06:52.000
resurrection would feel cheap with the
way things were left but a ghost version

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.800
