wouldn't surprise me at all. and that's

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:00.400
the overview of what happened
tic's blood relation to titus

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:04.479
braithwhite was what set things in
motion. his distant cousin samuel

00:07:04.479 --> 00:07:08.560
braithwight wanted to use him
and his blood to achieve immortality.

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:12.000
they imprisoned
montrose to lure tic to ardham and he

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.080
brought his uncle george
and his childhood friend letticia into it.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:20.479
in the end things didn't work out for
samuel who died alongside the other sons

00:07:20.479 --> 00:07:24.639
of adam at the ceremony but the order of
the ancient dawn still has

00:07:24.639 --> 00:07:29.440
other lodges throughout the country. his
daughter christina also survived and she

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:32.560
